ge look  that I i define pretty early on pretty  much before even started writing and  we've stuck to that there hasn't been  really many changes having my team  helped me to with some of the research  and some of the quotes and doing some of  the interviews to me is also really  helped alleviate the stuff that I'm not  as passionate about so my my short  answer is probably but I'm hedging a  little bit let's see how the first one  does see if I I like it for me it's  really a challenge of opportunity right  there's so many opportunities I can work  on writing the book takes up an insane  amount of time and should I be doing  that or should I be hosting a TV show  should I be investing into businesses  should I be starting the incubator  should I be creating an entrepreneur  cafe should I be making Toronto the best  city in the world for entrepreneurs like  there's a lot of demands on my time from  a business point of view and I have to  decide where is where is it going to  have the biggest impact and number three  is the book turning out as good as you  hoped it would be I'm pretty happy with  it by next week I should have the the  rough draft finished and then I'm going  to be editing going through going  through going through its kind of  refined but so far so good I'm really  excited next up Dominic  Tina who asked hey Evan its it's awesome  how guys YouTube notice all the hard  work you creativity put in your true  inspiration I do have one question it's  not exactly about book but similar I  want to get people to sign up for my  free online video happiness course I  created where I can give them way more  value than just in YouTube I tried  facebook twitter youtube vids but still  have low attention and people are not  willing to sign up what would you  recommend to get more people in I think  the free course gives tremendous value  and I want to help them as much as  possible I think what you need to do is  kick up as much noise in your industry  as possible